Z||000000||jerpro||01-03-2001||06:00 PM||||has anyone bought anything from west coast fieros?<BR>I am interested in the "forza" seat.  <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com/Seats/Other_car_seats.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cwestco.com/Seats/Other_car_seats.html</A> <BR>any idea if there is a similar seat I could buy cheaper or a better seat? (in blue)<BR>Second question.<BR>I am plannig on painting the interior of my car (dash and so forth) what kind of paint should I use?<BR>should I sand the dash before i paint? or can I leave the black color on it?( this is an ignorant question) <BR>thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||stimpy||01-03-2001||06:18 PM||||My dad had his ACE 3.8 conversion corrected by West Coast. Chris West has a similar tempermant to our friend Archie, in that he is a perfectionist and is not one to make compromises. <BR>That being said, West Coast is nt a high volume retail establishment. Can you get your seats cheaper? I don't doubt it.  But if you buy something from Chris, it <B>will</B> fit.  Try getting that kind of assurance from the guy working down at the local speed shop.||||reg||1
Z||000002||jerpro||01-03-2001||11:32 PM||||does anyone know what is the best kind of paint to use on the dash board of the fieros?<BR>c'mon out of the dozens of member no one knows?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||01-03-2001||11:37 PM||||SEM makes a good quality vinyl/plasic paint.  You can buy pre-mixed colors in most paint shops and even some discount stores (K-Mart, etc.).<P>There is a paint shop here in Denver that can custom mix colors.  I had them mix me up some '88 tan (medium beechwood, light sienna, dark sienna, etc.).<P><BR>The pre mixed aerosol cans are about $6, but the custom colors are A LOT more. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||80's BOY||01-03-2001||11:37 PM||||they make a vinyl paint. i can't remember the name of the brand, but there's some good one's out there. scuff all parts with a scotch pad or 1000 grit wet sand them first.||||reg||1
